# ---------------------------------------------------------------- python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
.venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- caches
.cache/
*.npy
*.npz

# ------------------------------------------------------- trained weights
# Regenerable by re-running the training script, and 0.5-22 MB each. The CSV
# logs under exp/results/ are the results worth keeping, not the checkpoints.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.safetensors

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- datasets
# Everything under data/ is fetched by a script, EXCEPT DRIVE which is small
# enough to have been committed. Written as a wildcard so a new dataset is
# ignored by default rather than accidentally committed at 100+ MB.
#   STARE       exp/fetch_stare.py   (19 MB, Clemson mirror)
#   HRF         exp/fetch_hrf.py     (76 MB, FAU mirror)
#   TopoMortar  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/jmlipman/TopoMortar.git data/TopoMortar
data/*
!data/DRIVE/

# Downloaded archives, wherever a fetch script leaves them.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# ------------------------------------------------------------ credentials
# Nothing here should ever exist in this repo; the pattern is a backstop.
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
token*.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- junk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.tmp
scratch/
tmp/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ results
# UNTRACKED FROM 2026-09-06, by Ivan's decision. exp/results/ was moved to
# /tmp2/ivanchang/ian_mei_results on 2026-09-03 to free 30 GB on the repo
# disk and replaced by a symlink; git then read all 2193 tracked result files
# as deleted on every status.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS. `git show HEAD:exp/results/...` no longer recovers a
# damaged table. That recovery was used for real on 2026-09-03, when a loop
# truncated checkpoint_scores.csv down to 1 run of 460.
#
# WHAT STILL WORKS. History is not rewritten. Everything committed up to
# 6f9a4ed is reachable by naming that commit:
#     git show 6f9a4ed:exp/results/heldout/checkpoint_scores.csv > out.csv
# (verified 2026-09-06: 72001 lines came back.) So the net is FROZEN, not
# gone. Results produced after 6f9a4ed live only on /tmp2 and git does not
# back them up -- treat that directory as the only copy.
exp/results
